# Face Match Benchmark

This directory contains a small, honest, re-runnable benchmark for the face-match pipeline
used in production (`face-api.js` FaceRecognitionNet descriptor extraction + cosine similarity
from `attendance-crypto.server.ts`).

## Dataset structure

Populate `benchmarks/dataset/` with real captured data (NOT synthetic):

```
benchmarks/dataset/
  subject_01/
    reference.jpg          # enrollment reference image (well-lit, frontal)
    normal_light.jpg       # probe: normal classroom lighting
    dim_light.jpg          # probe: dim lighting
    side_light.jpg         # probe: side lighting
    with_glasses.jpg       # probe: wearing glasses
  subject_02/
    reference.jpg
    ...
```

Each subject folder must contain exactly one file with `reference` in its name. All other
image files in the folder are treated as probes. The condition label is the filename without
the extension (e.g. `dim_light.jpg` → condition `dim_light`).

## Running

```bash
node scripts/benchmark-face-match.mjs
```

Optional args:

```bash
node scripts/benchmark-face-match.mjs --dataset benchmarks/dataset --out benchmarks
```

## Outputs

- `benchmarks/results.csv` — per-probe: subject, condition, similarity, decision
- `benchmarks/results.json` — same data as JSON + summary stats
- stdout summary — overall match rate, false-reject estimate, per-condition breakdown

## Honest scope

This is a small pilot benchmark. It does NOT claim demographic breakdowns unless the dataset
actually includes that variation. It reports only what the collected data supports. The
thresholds used (`THRESHOLD_MATCH = 0.82`, `THRESHOLD_REVIEW = 0.75`) are the same as in
`src/lib/attendance.functions.ts` — this benchmark directly informs whether those thresholds
are appropriate for this system's actual camera/lighting/population conditions.